{"toolCallId":"call_9eb9fa0e20d54017861c9ca957ac9ab9","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json:15:    \"rule_id\": \"PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\",\n=== registry entry ===\nES_EXISTS\"],\"script_path\":\"rules/check-files.sh\",\"severity\":\"error\",\"category\":\"authored_template\",\"description\":\"Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\"},{\"rule_id\":\"PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\",\"aliases\":[\"PLACEHOLDER\",\"PLACEHOLDERS\",\"PLACEHOLDERS_FILLED\"],\"script_path\":\"rules/check-placeholders.sh\",\"severity\":\"error\",\"category\":\"authored_template\",\"description\":\"Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\"},{\"rule_id\":\"COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER\",\"aliases\":[\"COMMENT_HYGIENE\"],\"script_path\":\"rules/check-comment-hygiene.sh\",\"severity\":\"error\",\"category\":\"authored_template\",\"description\":\"Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\"},{\"rule_id\":\"SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED\",\"aliases\":[\"SCAFFOLD_MARKERS\",\"TEMPLATE_SCAFFOLD\"],\"script_path\":\"rules/check-scaffold-never-touched.sh\",\"severity\":\"error\",\"category\":\"authored_template\",\"description\":\"Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\"},{\"rule_id\":\"STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY\",\"aliases\":[\"STATUS_CONSISTENCY\",\"CROSS_DOC_STATUS\"],\"script_path\":\"rules/check-status-cross-doc-consistency.sh\",\"severity\":\"error\",\"category\":\"authored_template\",\"description\":\"Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\"},{\"rule_id\":\"LEVEL_DECLARED\",\"aliases\":[\"LEVEL\"],\"script_path\":\"rules/check-level.sh\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"category\":\"authored_template\",\"description\":\"Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\"},{\"rule_id\":\"AC_COVERA\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"69e806","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_a63a638bc64945fe98526564a857c1ad","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: RECOMMEND LEVEL\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# SpecKit Level Recommendation Algorithm\n#\n# PURPOSE:\n#   Automated level recommendation that replaces soft LOC guidance with\n#   Deterministic scoring. Analyzes task complexity factors and recommends\n#   The appropriate SpecKit level (0-3).\n#\n# USAGE:\n#   Recommend-level.sh [OPTIONS]\n#\n# OPTIONS:\n#   --loc <number>       Lines of code estimate\n#   --files <number>     Number of files to modify\n#   --auth               Task involves authentication/authorization changes\n#   --api                Task involves API changes\n#   --db                 Task involves database changes\n#   --architectural      Task involves architectural changes\n#   --recommend-phases   Include phase scoring in output (default behavior)\n#   --no-recommend-phases  Disable phase scoring output\n#   --phase-threshold <N> Override phase score threshold (default 25)\n#   --json, -j           Output in JSON format\n#   --help, -h           Show this help message\n#\n# EXAMPLES:\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --db\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n#\n# SCORING ALGORITHM:\n#   LOC Factor:        35% weight (0-35 points)\n#   File Count:        20% weight (0-20 points)\n#   Risk Factors:      25% weight (auth +10, api +8, db +7)\n#   Complexity:        20% weight (architectural +20)\n#\n# LEVEL MAPPING:\n#   Public vocabulary remains level-only; internal template routing is not surfaced here.\n#   <25 points  -> Level 0 (Quick)\n#   25-44       -> Level 1 (Baseline)\n#   45-69       -> Level 2 (Verification)\n#   70+         -> Level 3 (Full)\n#\n# PHASE SCORING (separate from level, enabled by default):\n#   Architectural flag:     +15 points\n#   Files > 15:             +10 points\n#   LOC > 800:              +10 points\n#   Risk flags >= 2:        +10 points\n#   Extreme scale bonus:    +5 points (Files > 30 OR LOC > 2000)\n#   Max phase score: 50\n#\n# PHASE RECOMMENDATION:\n#   Score >= 25 AND Level >= 3 -> phases recommended\n#   Score 25-34: 2 phases suggested\n#   Score 35-44: 3 phases suggested\n#   Score 45+:   4+ phases suggested\n#\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 1. CONFIGURATION\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Weight configuration (percentages)\nreadonly WEIGHT_LOC=35\nreadonly WEIGHT_FILES=20\nreadonly WEIGHT_RISK=25\nreadonly WEIGHT_COMPLEXITY=20\n\n# Risk factor points (within WEIGHT_RISK budget)\nreadonly POINTS_AUTH=10\nreadonly POINTS_API=8\nreadonly POINTS_DB=7\n\n# Complexity points (within WEIGHT_COMPLEXITY budget)\nreadonly POINTS_ARCHITECTURAL=20\n\n# Phase signal scoring (separate from level scoring)\n# Max phase score = 50 (10+10+10+10+10)\nreadonly PHASE_POINTS_ARCHITECTURAL=10\nreadonly PHASE_POINTS_MANY_FILES=10      # Files > 15\nreadonly PHASE_POINTS_LARGE_LOC=10       # LOC > 800\nreadonly PHASE_POINTS_MULTI_RISK=10      # Risk flags >= 2\nreadonly PHASE_POINTS_EXTREME_SCALE=10   # Files > 30 OR LOC > 2000 (concrete thresholds for \"exceeds any dimension by 2x+\")\nreadonly PHASE_MAX_SCORE=50\nreadonly PHASE_DEFAULT_THRESHOLD=25\n\n# LOC thresholds for scoring\nreadonly LOC_THRESHOLD_LOW=50\nreadonly LOC_THRESHOLD_MED=150\nreadonly LOC_THRESHOLD_HIGH=400\nreadonly LOC_THRESHOLD_MAX=1000\n\n# File count thresholds\nreadonly FILES_THRESHOLD_LOW=3\nreadonly FILES_THRESHOLD_MED=8\nreadonly FILES_THRESHOLD_HIGH=15\nreadonly FILES_THRESHOLD_MAX=30\n\n# Level thresholds\nreadonly LEVEL_0_MAX=24\nreadonly LEVEL_1_MAX=44\nreadonly LEVEL_2_MAX=69\n# 70+ = Level 3\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 2. GLOBALS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nLOC=0\nFILES=0\nHAS_AUTH=false\nHAS_API=false\nHAS_DB=false\nHAS_ARCHITECTURAL=false\nJSON_OUTPUT=false\n\n# Phase recommendation flags\nRECOMMEND_PHASES=true\nPHASE_THRESHOLD=$PHASE_DEFAULT_THRESHOLD\n\n# Calculated scores\nSCORE_LOC=0\nSCORE_FILES=0\nSCORE_RISK=0\nSCORE_COMPLEXITY=0\nTOTAL_SCORE=0\nRECOMMENDED_LEVEL=0\nLEVEL_NAME=\"\"\nCONFIDENCE=0\n\n# Phase scoring results\nPHASE_SCORE=0\nPHASE_RECOMMENDED=false\nPHASE_REASON=\"\"\nSUGGESTED_PHASE_COUNT=0\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 3. HELPER FUNCTIONS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# _json_escape(string)\n# Escape characters that would break JSON string values\n_json_escape() {\n  local s=\"$1\"\n  s=\"${s//\\\\/\\\\\\\\}\"\n  s=\"${s//\\\"/\\\\\\\"}\"\n  s=\"${s//$'\\n'/\\\\n}\"\n  s=\"${s//$'\\r'/\\\\r}\"\n  s=\"${s//$'\\t'/\\\\t}\"\n  printf '%s' \"$s\"\n}\n\n# Show_help()\n# Display usage information\nshow_help() {\n  cat << 'EOF'\nSpecKit Level Recommendation Algorithm\n\nAnalyzes task complexity factors and recommends the appropriate SpecKit level.\n\nUSAGE:\n  recommend-level.sh [OPTIONS]\n\nOPTIONS:\n  --loc <number>       Lines of code estimate (required)\n  --files <number>     Number of files to modify (required)\n  --auth               Task involves authentication/authorization changes\n  --api                Task involves API changes\n  --db                 Task involves database changes\n  --architectural      Task involves architectural changes\n  --recommend-phases   Include phase scoring in output (default)\n  --no-recommend-phases Disable phase scoring output\n  --phase-threshold <N> Override phase score threshold (default 25)\n  --json, -j           Output in JSON format\n  --help, -h           Show this help message\n\nEXAMPLES:\n  # Simple task\n  recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2\n\n  # Medium complexity with API\n  recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api\n\n  # Complex full-stack feature\n  recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n\n  # With phase recommendation (default behavior)\n  recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n\n  # Disable phase recommendation fields\n  recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases\n\n  # JSON output for scripting\n  recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json\n\nLEVELS:\n  Level 0 (Quick):        <25 points  - Trivial changes, no formal spec needed\n  Level 1 (Baseline):     25-44       - Standard tasks, basic documentation\n  Level 2 (Verification): 45-69       - Complex tasks, full verification needed\n  Level 3 (Full):         70+         - Critical/architectural, comprehensive docs\n\nEOF\n  exit 0\n}\n\n# Calculate_loc_score()\n# Calculate points for LOC factor (0-35 points)\n# Uses linear interpolation between thresholds\ncalculate_loc_score() {\n  local loc=$1\n  local score=0\n\n  if [[ \"$loc\" -le \"$LOC_THRESHOLD_LOW\" ]]; then\n    # 0-50 LOC: 0-8 points (linear)\n    score=$((loc * 8 / LOC_THRESHOLD_LOW))\n  elif [[ \"$loc\" -le \"$LOC_THRESHOLD_MED\" ]]; then\n    # 51-150 LOC: 8-18 points\n    local range=$((LOC_THRESHOLD_MED - LOC_THRESHOLD_LOW))\n    local offset=$((loc - LOC_THRESHOLD_LOW))\n    score=$((8 + (offset * 10 / range)))\n  elif [[ \"$loc\" -le \"$LOC_THRESHOLD_HIGH\" ]]; then\n    # 151-400 LOC: 18-28 points\n    local range=$((LOC_THRESHOLD_HIGH - LOC_THRESHOLD_MED))\n    local offset=$((loc - LOC_THRESHOLD_MED))\n    score=$((18 + (offset * 10 / range)))\n  elif [[ \"$loc\" -le \"$LOC_THRESHOLD_MAX\" ]]; then\n    # 401-1000 LOC: 28-35 points\n    local range=$((LOC_THRESHOLD_MAX - LOC_THRESHOLD_HIGH))\n    local offset=$((loc - LOC_THRESHOLD_HIGH))\n    score=$((28 + (offset * 7 / range)))\n  else\n    # >1000 LOC: max points\n    score=$WEIGHT_LOC\n  fi\n\n  # Ensure score doesn't exceed weight\n  if [[ \"$score\" -gt \"$WEIGHT_LOC\" ]]; then\n    score=$WEIGHT_LOC\n  fi\n\n  echo \"$score\"\n}\n\n# Calculate_files_score()\n# Calculate points for file count factor (0-20 points)\ncalculate_files_score() {\n  local files=$1\n  local score=0\n\n  if [[ \"$files\" -le \"$FILES_THRESHOLD_LOW\" ]]; then\n    # 1-3 files: 0-5 points\n    score=$((files * 5 / FILES_THRESHOLD_LOW))\n  elif [[ \"$files\" -le \"$FILES_THRESHOLD_MED\" ]]; then\n    # 4-8 files: 5-10 points\n    local range=$((FILES_THRESHOLD_MED - FILES_THRESHOLD_LOW))\n    local offset=$((files - FILES_THRESHOLD_LOW))\n    score=$((5 + (offset * 5 / range)))\n  elif [[ \"$files\" -le \"$FILES_THRESHOLD_HIGH\" ]]; then\n    # 9-15 files: 10-16 points\n    local range=$((FILES_THRESHOLD_HIGH - FILES_THRESHOLD_MED))\n    local offset=$((files - FILES_THRESHOLD_MED))\n    score=$((10 + (offset * 6 / range)))\n  elif [[ \"$files\" -le \"$FILES_THRESHOLD_MAX\" ]]; then\n    # 16-30 files: 16-20 points\n    local range=$((FILES_THRESHOLD_MAX - FILES_THRESHOLD_HIGH))\n    local offset=$((files - FILES_THRESHOLD_HIGH))\n    score=$((16 + (offset * 4 / range)))\n  else\n    # >30 files: max points\n    score=$WEIGHT_FILES\n  fi\n\n  # Ensure score doesn't exceed weight\n  if [[ \"$score\" -gt \"$WEIGHT_FILES\" ]]; then\n    score=$WEIGHT_FILES\n  fi\n\n  echo \"$score\"\n}\n\n# Calculate_risk_score()\n# Calculate points for risk factors (0-25 points)\ncalculate_risk_score() {\n  local score=0\n\n  if [[ \"$HAS_AUTH\" = true ]]; then\n    score=$((score + POINTS_AUTH))\n  fi\n\n  if [[ \"$HAS_API\" = true ]]; then\n    score=$((score + POINTS_API))\n  fi\n\n  if [[ \"$HAS_DB\" = true ]]; then\n    score=$((score + POINTS_DB))\n  fi\n\n  # Cap at WEIGHT_RISK\n  if [[ \"$score\" -gt \"$WEIGHT_RISK\" ]]; then\n    score=$WEIGHT_RISK\n  fi\n\n  echo \"$score\"\n}\n\n# Calculate_complexity_score()\n# Calculate points for complexity factors (0-20 points)\ncalculate_complexity_score() {\n  local score=0\n\n  if [[ \"$HAS_ARCHITECTURAL\" = true ]]; then\n    score=$((score + POINTS_ARCHITECTURAL))\n  fi\n\n  # Cap at WEIGHT_COMPLEXITY\n  if [[ \"$score\" -gt \"$WEIGHT_COMPLEXITY\" ]]; then\n    score=$WEIGHT_COMPLEXITY\n  fi\n\n  echo \"$score\"\n}\n\n# Determine_level()\n# Map total score to recommended level\ndetermine_level() {\n  local score=$1\n\n  if [[ \"$score\" -le \"$LEVEL_0_MAX\" ]]; then\n    RECOMMENDED_LEVEL=0\n    LEVEL_NAME=\"Quick\"\n  elif [[ \"$score\" -le \"$LEVEL_1_MAX\" ]]; then\n    RECOMMENDED_LEVEL=1\n    LEVEL_NAME=\"Baseline\"\n  elif [[ \"$score\" -le \"$LEVEL_2_MAX\" ]]; then\n    RECOMMENDED_LEVEL=2\n    LEVEL_NAME=\"Verification\"\n  else\n    RECOMMENDED_LEVEL=3\n    LEVEL_NAME=\"Full\"\n  fi\n}\n\n# Determine_phasing()\n# Calculate phase recommendation score and suggested phase count.\n# Phase scoring is SEPARATE from level scoring — uses its own 5 signal\n# Dimensions (max 50 points). Phase is recommended when:\n#   - Phase score >= PHASE_THRESHOLD (default 25)\n#   - AND RECOMMENDED_LEVEL >= 3\n# Must be called AFTER determine_level() since it references RECOMMENDED_LEVEL.\ndetermine_phasing() {\n  PHASE_SCORE=0\n  PHASE_REASON=\"\"\n  PHASE_RECOMMENDED=false\n  SUGGESTED_PHASE_COUNT=0\n\n  local reasons=\"\"\n  local risk_flag_count=0\n\n  # Signal 1: Architectural flag (+10)\n  if [[ \"$HAS_ARCHITECTURAL\" = true ]]; then\n    PHASE_SCORE=$((PHASE_SCORE + PHASE_POINTS_ARCHITECTURAL))\n    reasons=\"Architectural change\"\n  fi\n\n  # Signal 2: Many files (+10) — Files > 15\n  if [[ \"$FILES\" -gt 15 ]]; then\n    PHASE_SCORE=$((PHASE_SCORE + PHASE_POINTS_MANY_FILES))\n    if [[ -n \"$reasons\" ]]; then\n      reasons=\"${reasons} + ${FILES} files\"\n    else\n      reasons=\"${FILES} files\"\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  # Signal 3: Large LOC (+10) — LOC > 800\n  if [[ \"$LOC\" -gt 800 ]]; then\n    PHASE_SCORE=$((PHASE_SCORE + PHASE_POINTS_LARGE_LOC))\n    if [[ -n \"$reasons\" ]]; then\n      reasons=\"${reasons} + ${LOC} LOC\"\n    else\n      reasons=\"${LOC} LOC\"\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  # Signal 4: Multi-domain risk (+10) — 2+ risk flags\n  if [[ \"$HAS_AUTH\" = true ]]; then risk_flag_count=$((risk_flag_count + 1)); fi\n  if [[ \"$HAS_API\" = true ]]; then risk_flag_count=$((risk_flag_count + 1)); fi\n  if [[ \"$HAS_DB\" = true ]]; then risk_flag_count=$((risk_flag_count + 1)); fi\n\n  if [[ \"$risk_flag_count\" -ge 2 ]]; then\n    PHASE_SCORE=$((PHASE_SCORE + PHASE_POINTS_MULTI_RISK))\n    # Build risk factor description\n    local risk_names=\"\"\n    if [[ \"$HAS_AUTH\" = true ]]; then risk_names=\"Auth\"; fi\n    if [[ \"$HAS_API\" = true ]]; then\n      if [[ -n \"$risk_names\" ]]; then risk_names=\"${risk_names} + API\"; else risk_names=\"API\"; fi\n    fi\n    if [[ \"$HAS_DB\" = true ]]; then\n      if [[ -n \"$risk_names\" ]]; then risk_names=\"${risk_names} + DB\"; else risk_names=\"DB\"; fi\n    fi\n    if [[ -n \"$reasons\" ]]; then\n      reasons=\"${reasons} + ${risk_names} risk factors\"\n    else\n      reasons=\"${risk_names} risk factors\"\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  # Signal 5: Extreme scale bonus (+10) — Files > 30 OR LOC > 2000 (concrete thresholds for \"exceeds any dimension by 2x+\")\n  if [[ \"$FILES\" -gt 30 ]] || [[ \"$LOC\" -gt 2000 ]]; then\n    PHASE_SCORE=$((PHASE_SCORE + PHASE_POINTS_EXTREME_SCALE))\n    if [[ -n \"$reasons\" ]]; then\n      reasons=\"${reasons} + extreme scale\"\n    else\n      reasons=\"Extreme scale\"\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  # Cap at max score\n  if [[ \"$PHASE_SCORE\" -gt \"$PHASE_MAX_SCORE\" ]]; then\n    PHASE_SCORE=$PHASE_MAX_SCORE\n  fi\n\n  PHASE_REASON=\"$reasons\"\n\n  # Phase recommendation requires BOTH score threshold AND level >= 3\n  if [[ \"$PHASE_SCORE\" -ge \"$PHASE_THRESHOLD\" ]] && [[ \"$RECOMMENDED_LEVEL\" -ge 3 ]]; then\n    PHASE_RECOMMENDED=true\n\n    # Determine suggested phase count based on score ranges\n    if [[ \"$PHASE_SCORE\" -ge 45 ]]; then\n      SUGGESTED_PHASE_COUNT=4\n    elif [[ \"$PHASE_SCORE\" -ge 35 ]]; then\n      SUGGESTED_PHASE_COUNT=3\n    else\n      # Score 25-34\n      SUGGESTED_PHASE_COUNT=2\n    fi\n  fi\n}\n\n# Calculate_confidence()\n# Calculate confidence percentage based on input completeness\ncalculate_confidence() {\n  local base_confidence=60\n  local bonus=0\n\n  # More inputs = higher confidence\n  if [[ \"$LOC\" -gt 0 ]]; then\n    bonus=$((bonus + 15))\n  fi\n\n  if [[ \"$FILES\" -gt 0 ]]; then\n    bonus=$((bonus + 15))\n  fi\n\n  # Risk factors add confidence when specified\n  local risk_factors=0\n  if [[ \"$HAS_AUTH\" = true ]]; then risk_factors=$((risk_factors + 1)); fi\n  if [[ \"$HAS_API\" = true ]]; then risk_factors=$((risk_factors + 1)); fi\n  if [[ \"$HAS_DB\" = true ]]; then risk_factors=$((risk_factors + 1)); fi\n  if [[ \"$HAS_ARCHITECTURAL\" = true ]]; then risk_factors=$((risk_factors + 1)); fi\n\n  # Each risk factor adds some confidence (shows thoroughness)\n  bonus=$((bonus + risk_factors * 2))\n\n  # If score is near threshold boundaries, reduce confidence\n  local distance_to_boundary=100\n  local boundaries=(\"$LEVEL_0_MAX\" \"$LEVEL_1_MAX\" \"$LEVEL_2_MAX\")\n  for boundary in \"${boundaries[@]}\"; do\n    local diff=$((TOTAL_SCORE - boundary))\n    if [[ \"$diff\" -lt 0 ]]; then diff=$((-diff)); fi\n    if [[ \"$diff\" -lt \"$distance_to_boundary\" ]]; then\n      distance_to_boundary=$diff\n    fi\n  done\n\n  # Reduce confidence if very close to a boundary (within 5 points)\n  if [[ \"$distance_to_boundary\" -le 5 ]]; then\n    bonus=$((bonus - 10))\n  fi\n\n  CONFIDENCE=$((base_confidence + bonus))\n\n  # Cap at 95% (never 100% certain)\n  if [[ \"$CONFIDENCE\" -gt 95 ]]; then\n    CONFIDENCE=95\n  fi\n\n  # Minimum 50%\n  if [[ \"$CONFIDENCE\" -lt 50 ]]; then\n    CONFIDENCE=50\n  fi\n}\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 4. OUTPUT FUNCTIONS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Output_text()\n# Output results in human-readable text format\noutput_text() {\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})\"\n  echo \"Score: ${TOTAL_SCORE}/100 | Confidence: ${CONFIDENCE}%\"\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"Breakdown:\"\n  echo \"- LOC (${LOC}): +${SCORE_LOC} points\"\n  echo \"- Files (${FILES}): +${SCORE_FILES} points\"\n  echo -n \"- API changes: \"\n  if [[ \"$HAS_API\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"+${POINTS_API} points\"\n  else\n    echo \"+0 points\"\n  fi\n  echo -n \"- Auth changes: \"\n  if [[ \"$HAS_AUTH\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"+${POINTS_AUTH} points\"\n  else\n    echo \"+0 points\"\n  fi\n  echo -n \"- DB changes: \"\n  if [[ \"$HAS_DB\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"+${POINTS_DB} points\"\n  else\n    echo \"+0 points\"\n  fi\n  echo -n \"- Architectural: \"\n  if [[ \"$HAS_ARCHITECTURAL\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"+${POINTS_ARCHITECTURAL} points\"\n  else\n    echo \"+0 points\"\n  fi\n  echo \"\"\n\n  # Phase recommendation section (default on; can be disabled with --no-recommend-phases)\n  if [[ \"$RECOMMEND_PHASES\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"Phase Recommendation:\"\n    echo \"- Phase Score: ${PHASE_SCORE}/${PHASE_MAX_SCORE} (threshold: ${PHASE_THRESHOLD})\"\n    if [[ \"$PHASE_RECOMMENDED\" = true ]]; then\n      echo \"- Recommended: YES\"\n      echo \"- Suggested Phases: ${SUGGESTED_PHASE_COUNT}\"\n      echo \"- Reason: ${PHASE_REASON}\"\n    else\n      echo \"- Recommended: NO\"\n      if [[ -n \"$PHASE_REASON\" ]]; then\n        echo \"- Factors: ${PHASE_REASON}\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    echo \"\"\n  fi\n}\n\n# Output_json()\n# Output results in JSON format\noutput_json() {\n  local auth_points=0\n  local api_points=0\n  local db_points=0\n  local arch_points=0\n\n  if [[ \"$HAS_AUTH\" = true ]]; then auth_points=$POINTS_AUTH; fi\n  if [[ \"$HAS_API\" = true ]]; then api_points=$POINTS_API; fi\n  if [[ \"$HAS_DB\" = true ]]; then db_points=$POINTS_DB; fi\n  if [[ \"$HAS_ARCHITECTURAL\" = true ]]; then arch_points=$POINTS_ARCHITECTURAL; fi\n\n  # Build JSON output — phase fields conditionally included\n  if [[ \"$RECOMMEND_PHASES\" = true ]]; then\n    cat << EOF\n{\n  \"recommended_level\": ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL},\n  \"level_name\": \"${LEVEL_NAME}\",\n  \"total_score\": ${TOTAL_SCORE},\n  \"max_score\": 100,\n  \"confidence\": ${CONFIDENCE},\n  \"recommended_phases\": ${PHASE_RECOMMENDED},\n  \"phase_score\": ${PHASE_SCORE},\n  \"phase_reason\": \"$(_json_escape \"${PHASE_REASON}\")\",\n  \"suggested_phase_count\": ${SUGGESTED_PHASE_COUNT},\n  \"inputs\": {\n    \"loc\": ${LOC},\n    \"files\": ${FILES},\n    \"auth\": ${HAS_AUTH},\n    \"api\": ${HAS_API},\n    \"db\": ${HAS_DB},\n    \"architectural\": ${HAS_ARCHITECTURAL}\n  },\n  \"breakdown\": {\n    \"loc_score\": ${SCORE_LOC},\n    \"files_score\": ${SCORE_FILES},\n    \"risk_score\": ${SCORE_RISK},\n    \"complexity_score\": ${SCORE_COMPLEXITY},\n    \"details\": {\n      \"auth_points\": ${auth_points},\n      \"api_points\": ${api_points},\n      \"db_points\": ${db_points},\n      \"architectural_points\": ${arch_points}\n    }\n  },\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"level_0_max\": ${LEVEL_0_MAX},\n    \"level_1_max\": ${LEVEL_1_MAX},\n    \"level_2_max\": ${LEVEL_2_MAX}\n  }\n}\nEOF\n  else\n    cat << EOF\n{\n  \"recommended_level\": ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL},\n  \"level_name\": \"${LEVEL_NAME}\",\n  \"total_score\": ${TOTAL_SCORE},\n  \"max_score\": 100,\n  \"confidence\": ${CONFIDENCE},\n  \"inputs\": {\n    \"loc\": ${LOC},\n    \"files\": ${FILES},\n    \"auth\": ${HAS_AUTH},\n    \"api\": ${HAS_API},\n    \"db\": ${HAS_DB},\n    \"architectural\": ${HAS_ARCHITECTURAL}\n  },\n  \"breakdown\": {\n    \"loc_score\": ${SCORE_LOC},\n    \"files_score\": ${SCORE_FILES},\n    \"risk_score\": ${SCORE_RISK},\n    \"complexity_score\": ${SCORE_COMPLEXITY},\n    \"details\": {\n      \"auth_points\": ${auth_points},\n      \"api_points\": ${api_points},\n      \"db_points\": ${db_points},\n      \"architectural_points\": ${arch_points}\n    }\n  },\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"level_0_max\": ${LEVEL_0_MAX},\n    \"level_1_max\": ${LEVEL_1_MAX},\n    \"level_2_max\": ${LEVEL_2_MAX}\n  }\n}\nEOF\n  fi\n}\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 5. MAIN SCRIPT\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Parse command-line arguments\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --loc)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      LOC=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --files)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --files requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      FILES=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --auth)\n      HAS_AUTH=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --api)\n      HAS_API=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --db)\n      HAS_DB=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --architectural)\n      HAS_ARCHITECTURAL=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --recommend-phases)\n      RECOMMEND_PHASES=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --no-recommend-phases)\n      RECOMMEND_PHASES=false\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --phase-threshold)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --phase-threshold requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      PHASE_THRESHOLD=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --json|-j)\n      JSON_OUTPUT=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --help|-h)\n      show_help\n      ;;\n    *)\n      echo \"ERROR: Unknown option: $1\" >&2\n      echo \"Use --help for usage information\" >&2\n      exit 1\n      ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\n# Validate numeric inputs first (before numeric comparison)\nif ! [[ \"$LOC\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nif ! [[ \"$FILES\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --files must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nif ! [[ \"$PHASE_THRESHOLD\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --phase-threshold must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Validate required inputs\nif [[ \"$LOC\" -eq 0 ]] && [[ \"$FILES\" -eq 0 ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided\" >&2\n  echo \"Use --help for usage information\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 6. CALCULATE SCORES\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nSCORE_LOC=$(calculate_loc_score \"$LOC\")\nSCORE_FILES=$(calculate_files_score \"$FILES\")\nSCORE_RISK=$(calculate_risk_score)\nSCORE_COMPLEXITY=$(calculate_complexity_score)\n\nTOTAL_SCORE=$((SCORE_LOC + SCORE_FILES + SCORE_RISK + SCORE_COMPLEXITY))\n\n# Determine recommended level\ndetermine_level \"$TOTAL_SCORE\"\n\n# Calculate confidence\ncalculate_confidence\n\n# Calculate phase recommendation (default on; opt-out via --no-recommend-phases)\nif [[ \"$RECOMMEND_PHASES\" = true ]]; then\n  determine_phasing\nfi\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 7. OUTPUT RESULTS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nif [[ \"$JSON_OUTPUT\" = true ]]; then\n  output_json\nelse\n  output_text\nfi\n\nexit 0\n\n# Exit codes:\n#   0 - Success\n#   1 - ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"42fde0","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_adbca1f3d7d24c099a4babd0cd56c8cb","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: CHECK-COMPLEXITY\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Sourced by validate.sh and compatible with strict mode.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Rule: COMPLEXITY_MATCH\n# Severity: warn\n# Description: Validates that declared complexity level matches actual content.\n#   Checks if spec content is appropriate for the declared level.\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 1. HELPER FUNCTIONS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Extract level from spec.md metadata\n_complexity_get_declared_level() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local spec_file=\"$folder/spec.md\"\n    if [[ -f \"$spec_file\" ]]; then\n        local level\n\n        # Pattern 0: SPECKIT_LEVEL marker (authoritative)\n        level=$(grep -oE '<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: *[123]\\+? *-->' \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '[123]\\+?' | head -1 || true)\n\n        # Pattern 1: Metadata table with bold key\n        if [[ -z \"$level\" ]]; then\n            level=$(grep -E '\\|\\s*\\*\\*Level\\*\\*\\s*\\|\\s*[123]\\+?\\s*\\|' \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '[123]\\+?' | head -1 || true)\n        fi\n\n        # Pattern 2: Metadata table without bold key\n        if [[ -z \"$level\" ]]; then\n            level=$(grep -E '\\|\\s*Level\\s*\\|\\s*[123]\\+?\\s*\\|' \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '[123]\\+?' | head -1 || true)\n        fi\n\n        # Pattern 3: Bullet metadata\n        if [[ -z \"$level\" ]]; then\n            level=$(grep -E '^\\- \\*\\*Level\\*\\*:[[:space:]]*[123]\\+?' \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '[123]\\+?' | head -1 || true)\n        fi\n\n        # Pattern 4: YAML frontmatter\n        if [[ -z \"$level\" ]]; then\n            level=$(grep -E '^level:[[:space:]]*[123]\\+?' \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '[123]\\+?' | head -1 || true)\n        fi\n\n        # Pattern 5: Anchored inline fallback\n        if [[ -z \"$level\" ]]; then\n            level=$(grep -E '^[Ll]evel[: ]+[123]\\+?' \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '[123]\\+?' | head -1 || true)\n        fi\n\n        echo \"$level\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Count user stories in spec.md\n_complexity_count_user_stories() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local spec_file=\"$folder/spec.md\"\n    if [[ -f \"$spec_file\" ]]; then\n        local count\n        count=$(grep -cE \"^### (User Story|US-)\" \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n        echo \"${count:-0}\"\n    else\n        echo \"0\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Count acceptance scenarios in spec.md\n_complexity_count_acceptance_scenarios() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local spec_file=\"$folder/spec.md\"\n    if [[ -f \"$spec_file\" ]]; then\n        local count\n        count=$(grep -cE \"\\*\\*Given\\*\\*|^[[:space:]]*[0-9]+\\.[[:space:]]+Given\\b\" \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n        echo \"${count:-0}\"\n    else\n        echo \"0\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Count phases, preferring plan.md and falling back to tasks.md.\n#\n# The core plan template hands phase ownership to tasks.md so a packet has one\n# source of truth for phase state rather than two that drift. Counting only\n# plan.md therefore reports zero for every packet built that way, and warns that\n# a packet with three phases has none.\n_complexity_count_phases() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"d69e0a","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_adc6c564752c44b7a7ea6cbad422d9e7","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"62-| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\n63-| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\n64:| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n67-\n68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n69-\n70-### AC_CLOSURE\n71-\n72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n73-\n74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n75-\n76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n77-\n78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n79-\n80-**Failure modes:**\n81-\n82-| Condition | Result |\n83-|---|---|\n84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n85-| A row marked `Waived` or `Superseded` naming no ADR | `fail` — an unbacked waiver is not a pass |\n86-| A criterion row that cannot be parsed, or an unbalanced code fence | `fail` — a dropped row would empty the table and close the packet |\n87-| Duplicate criterion ids | `fail` — the tally is ambiguous |\n88-| A row citing an ADR that `decision-record.md` does not contain | `fail` — the record is the whole justification |\n89-| A packet claiming completion with an `Unmet` row | `fail` — this is the closure gate |\n--\n764-\n765-**Severity:** ERROR past 4,000 characters (the one limit, with no warning tier below it), ERROR for a missing binding child  \n766:**Rule:** `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY`, diagnostics `SPECDOC_SUFFICIENCY_005` (budget) and `SPECDOC_SUFFICIENCY_006` (binding)  \n767-**Description:** A packet `goal.md` carries the directive an operator sets as the session objective. Every runtime goal surface caps what it holds and truncates at the tail, where the completion criteria live, so the slice that gets set has a budget.\n768-\n769-### What Is Measured\n770-\n771-The durable slice: everything after the frontmatter's closing `---` up to `<!-- ANCHOR:log -->`, anchors and comments included, counted in characters. The frontmatter is never part of it and never leaves the file. The log is volatile and never part of it.\n772-\n773-### Where It Applies\n774-\n775-- **Phase parents** and **top-level packets**: one limit of 4,000 characters. Up to 4,000 passes with no diagnostic; past it fails. These are the documents an operator sets. A folder that resolves to the phase level counts as a phase parent even when it sits inside another packet.\n776-- **Phase children** that are not themselves phase parents: unbounded. A child binds through its parent and is never set directly.\n777-\n778-The goal command and `check-goal.cjs` draw the same line. Section 2 of sk-create-goal's [budget-and-handoff.md](../../../sk-doc/sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md) states it for goal authors.\n779-\n780-The limit lives in `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` as `goalDurableBudget.errorChars`, which the validator and the goal command read, and which the template and this reference quote.\n781-\n782-### Binding Rows\n783-\n784-On a phase parent the `binding` anchor lists each child's goal document. Every row's path must exist on disk. A row naming a child `goal.md` that was never authored is an error: the parent promises a directive the child cannot supply.\n785-\n786-### Examples\n787-\n788-❌ **Fail:** a parent `goal.md` whose slice measures 4,120 characters.\n789-\n790-```\n791-SPECDOC_SUFFICIENCY_005: goal.md: durable slice is 4120 characters (> 4000). Cut it in the order section 3 of sk-create-goal's references/budget-and-handoff.md gives, and never drop a criterion.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"633cff","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_b0eebacfec6543ab886e2817f08dd59d","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"total 112\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 michelkerkmeester  wheel    320 26 Oct 14:50 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 14:50 ..\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   3608 26 Oct 14:50 acceptance-criteria.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel    423 26 Oct 14:50 description.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   5412 26 Oct 14:50 graph-metadata.json\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   3672 26 Oct 14:50 implementation-summary.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  11692 26 Oct 14:50 plan.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 14:50 scratch\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   8336 26 Oct 14:50 spec.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  10842 26 Oct 14:50 tasks.md\n---SPEC---\n---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Write three sentences: the problem, the change and the proof. GOOD: Callers parse a 17-line report to read one value. The flag prints one line. A line count proves it. WEAK: This document describes the feature. -->\n\n[2-3 sentence high-level overview for stakeholders who need quick context]\n\n**Key Decisions**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Major decision 1], [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Major decision 2]\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Blocking dependency]\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/recommend-level-quiet`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: P0/P1/P2] |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The recommend-level script prints a 17-line report, so a caller that needs only the level cannot parse the answer. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\n\n### Purpose\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: One-sentence outcome statement. What does success look like?]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. GOOD: Add a `--quiet` flag that prints only the recommended-level line. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->\n\n### In Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 2]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 3]\n\n### Out of Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 1] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 2] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path/to/file.js] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Modify/Create/Delete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Write one testable requirement per row. Name the exact command or output. GOOD: With `--quiet`, stdout holds exactly one line that starts with `Recommended Level:`. WEAK: The flag should work well. -->\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-002 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line and exits 0. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n\n- **SC-001**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Primary measurable outcome]\n- **SC-002**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Secondary measurable outcome]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Name one dependency and one risk. Give each a concrete mitigation. GOOD: A caller parses the level line and breaks when the label changes. Mitigation: keep the label stable and test it. WEAK: There may be some risk. -->\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/API] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What if blocked] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback plan] |\n| Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: High/Med/Low] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Mitigation strategy] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Name one measurable limit per line. Write `N/A` and one reason when the packet runs no service, or delete the whole section. GOOD: The flag adds no measurable time: the same 40 ms run. WEAK: Performance is good. -->\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Response time target - e.g., <200ms p95]\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Auth requirement - e.g., JWT tokens required]\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Uptime target - e.g., 99.9%]\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n<!-- FILL: Name the empty input, the maximum input and the failure path. One line each. GOOD: Empty input: the script exits 2 with usage. Maximum: 10,000 files scores in under one second. WEAK: Handle edge cases. -->\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How system handles]\n- Maximum length: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Limit and behavior]\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback behavior]\n- Network timeout: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Retry strategy]\n\n### State Transitions\n- Partial completion: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Recovery behavior]\n- Session expiry: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User experience]\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n<!-- FILL: Score each row with the number the change earns. The total must match the level. GOOD: Scope 4/25: one file and 12 lines. Total 18/100. WEAK: Complexity is medium. -->\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /25] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Files: X, LOC: Y, Systems: Z] |\n| Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /25] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Auth: Y/N, API: Y/N, Breaking: Y/N] |\n| Research | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /20] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Investigation needs] |\n| Multi-Agent | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /15] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Workstreams: X] |\n| Coordination | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /15] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Dependencies: X] |\n| **Total** | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /100]** | **Level 3** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n<!-- FILL: List each risk with impact, likelihood and one mitigation. GOOD: R1: a caller parses the label. Impact M, likelihood L. Mitigation: a test pins the label. WEAK: Some risks exist. -->\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: H/M/L] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: H/M/L] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Strategy] |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n<!-- FILL: Write one story per user. Name the actor, the want and the benefit. GOOD: As a build script, I want one parseable line, so that I can skip the report. WEAK: Users want a quiet mode. -->\n\n### US-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Title] (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: user type], **I want** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: needed behavior], **so that** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: benefit].\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Title] (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: user type], **I want** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: needed behavior], **so that** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: benefit].\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n<!-- FILL: Write each open question as one line. Write `None` when nothing blocks. GOOD: Does `--quiet` suppress warnings? No, stderr is unchanged. WEAK: Edge cases are unclear. -->\n\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 1 requiring clarification]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 2 requiring clarification]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Leave the four links in place. -->\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"74148a","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_cf1b5eba2e6d4a0b9d2d2ffe4a5519ed","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: CHECK-PLACEHOLDERS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Sourced by validate.sh and compatible with strict mode.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n_placeholder_rule_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\n# shellcheck source=../lib/status-classifier.sh\nsource \"${_placeholder_rule_dir}/../lib/status-classifier.sh\"\n\n# Rule: PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\n# Severity: error\n# Description: Detects unfilled spec-doc placeholders: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE:], [NEEDS_CLARIFICATION:] / [NEEDS CLARIFICATION:],\n#   and a [template:...] provenance token left in a title line. Bracketed authoring hints such as [Decision Title]\n#   are soft by design and belong to spec/check-placeholders.sh, the standalone report.\n# Lifecycle: a doc whose SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE stamp is v2.3 or later ships every authoring hint as a\n#   [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...] token. While spec.md has the Status Draft, an unfilled token in such a doc is a\n#   warning. At any other status it is an error. A doc with an older stamp, or none, keeps the error it\n#   always had. [NEEDS_CLARIFICATION:] is an error in every packet.\n# Parity: mirrors the runtime orchestrator validatePlaceholders. Mustache {{...}} is NOT flagged\n# (not canonical spec-doc placeholder syntax; legit spec-doc content uses it).\n# The post-edit hook runs the broader bracket scan at spec/check-placeholders.sh\n# instead; that one catches leftovers of upgrade-level, this one gates closure.\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 1. HELPERS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Succeeds when the doc carries a SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE stamp of v2.3 or later\n# within its first 70 lines. A doc with an older stamp, or none, fails.\ncarries_token_gate_stamp() {\n    local filepath=\"$1\"\n    local stamp_line major minor\n    stamp_line=$(head -n 70 \"$filepath\" 2>/dev/null | \\\n        grep -m1 -E '^[[:space:]]*<!--[[:space:]]*SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE:[^|>]*\\|[[:space:]]*v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+[[:space:]]*-->' || true)\n    [[ -n \"$stamp_line\" ]] || return 1\n    major=$(printf '%s' \"$stamp_line\" | sed -E 's/.*\\|[[:space:]]*v([0-9]+)\\.([0-9]+).*/\\1/')\n    minor=$(printf '%s' \"$stamp_line\" | sed -E 's/.*\\|[[:space:]]*v([0-9]+)\\.([0-9]+).*/\\2/')\n    if (( major > 2 )) || { (( major == 2 )) && (( minor >= 3 )); }; then\n        return 0\n    fi\n    return 1\n}\n\n# Succeeds when the Status row of spec.md holds exactly the word Draft.\nspec_status_is_draft() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local value\n    value=\"$(extract_status_table_value \"$folder/spec.md\")\"\n    [[ \"$(speckit_status_trim \"$value\")\" == \"draft\" ]]\n}\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 2. INITIALIZATION\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nrun_check() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local level=\"$2\"\n    \n    RULE_NAME=\"PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\"\n    RULE_STATUS=\"pass\"\n    RULE_MESSAGE=\"\"\n    RULE_DETAILS=()\n    RULE_REMEDIATION=\"\"\n    \n    local -a files=(\"spec.md\" \"plan.md\" \"tasks.md\")\n    [[ -f \"$folder/decision-record.md\" ]] && files+=(\"decision-record.md\")\n    # These three are read only when they carry the token-gate stamp, so a doc\n    # with an older stamp is scanned exactly as it was before.\n    files+=(\"acceptance-criteria.md\" \"implementation-summary.md\" \"goal.md\")\n    \n    local -a found_placeholders=()\n    local -a draft_tokens=()\n    local draft_packet=false\n    if spec_status_is_draft \"$folder\"; then\n        draft_packet=true\n    fi\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 3. VALIDATION LOGIC\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    for file in \"${files[@]}\"; do\n        local filepath=\"$folder/$file\"\n        [[ ! -f \"$filepath\" ]] && continue\n        \n        # Skip: scratch/, memory/, templates/\n        if [[ \"$filepath\" == *\"/scratch/\"* ]] || \\\n           [[ \"$filepath\" == *\"/memory/\"* ]] || \\\n           [[ \"$filepath\" == *\"/templates/\"* ]]; then\n            continue\n        fi\n        \n        if type -t should_skip_path &>/dev/null; then\n            if should_skip_path \"$filepath\"; then\n                continue\n            fi\n        fi\n\n        local token_gated=false\n        if carries_token_gate_stamp \"$filepath\"; then\n            token_gated=true\n        fi\n        case \"$file\" in\n            acceptance-criteria.md|implementation-summary.md|goal.md)\n                [[ \"$token_gated\" == true ]] || continue\n                ;;\n        esac\n        \n        # Filter out fenced code blocks\n        local filtered\n        filtered=$(awk '\n            BEGIN { in_code = 0 }\n            /^```/ { in_code = !in_code; next }\n            !in_code { print NR \":\" $0 }\n        ' \"$filepath\" 2>/dev/null)\n        \n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"e14c5f","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_d4d1d4aa65294fe485260246f8c8048f","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"repaired specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n    packet pointer -> zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n    re-derive graph metadata\n\ninspected=1 repaired=1 failed=0\n\nNot repairable here — these record work someone did, and only they can write them:\n      1  AI_PROTOCOLS\n      1  PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"7bef48","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_da3874a8cacc4695a4c980bc8625be9a","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"=====PLAN=====\n---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"277c3e","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
